1
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:06,000
A comedy thriller about four men, a wedding and everybody's funeral.

2
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:06,000
Best Men is a comedy, romance film directed by Tamra Davis.

3
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:06,000
Four tuxedo clad men show up at a penitentiary to meet a friend who has just been released after
three years in prison and is going straight from the jail to marry his girlfriend.

4
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:06,000
En route to the wedding, one of the men asks to
stop by a bank to pick up some cash.

5
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:06,000
As it turns out, he is a wanted bank robber who uses Shakespeare passages
during his robberies and thus has become known as "Hamlet".

6
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:06,000
Soon all five men are caught up in the bank and involved in the
robbery as they end up in a hostage situation.

7
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:06,000
The hostage negotiator shows up who turns out to be Hamlet's father.

8
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:06,000
Buzz, played by Dean Cain.

9
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:06,000
Hope, played by Drew Barrymore.

10
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:06,000
Jesse, played by Luke Wilson.

11
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:06,000
Taddy, played by Andy Dick.

12
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Billy, played by Sean Patrick Flanery.

13
00:39:00,000 --> 00:39:06,000
Sol, played by Mitchell Whitfield.

14
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:06,000
Men in Black (abbreviated as MIB) is a 1997 American science fiction action comedy film directed by Barry Sonnenfeld,
based on a script by Ed Solomon, that adapts the Marvel Comics series The Men in Black by Lowell Cunningham.

15
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Tommy Lee Jones and Will Smith respectively star as Agent K and Agent J, who investigate a series of
seemingly unrelated criminal incidents related to the extraterrestrials who live in secret on Earth.

16
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
Linda Fiorentino, Vincent D'Onofrio, and Rip Torn
also appear in supporting roles.

17
00:51:00,000 --> 00:51:06,000
Development for the film began in 1992, after producers Walter F.

18
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
Parkes and Laurie MacDonald optioned the rights to the comic book series.

19
00:57:00,000 --> 00:57:06,000
Solomon was soon hired to write the screenplay; Sonnenfeld was the preferred directorial choice, which resulted in
delays due to his commitments to other film projects and a failure to secure any alternative directors.

20
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
Principal photography began in March 1996 and lasted until that June,
with filming primarily taking place in New York City.

21
01:03:00,000 --> 01:03:06,000
The film's visual effects were helmed by Industrial Light & Magic.

22
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
The film's soundtrack contains the theme song of the same name, performed
by Smith, as well as the score, composed by Danny Elfman.

23
01:09:00,000 --> 01:09:06,000
Men in Black premiered at Pacific's Cinerama Dome in Hollywood on June 25, 1997, and was theatrically released
in the United States on July 2 by Sony Pictures Releasing through the Columbia Pictures label.

24
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
It received critical acclaim for its screenplay, humour, action sequences,
and the performances and chemistry between Jones and Smith.

25
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
The film was a box-office success, grossing more than $589.4 million worldwide and becoming the
third-highest-grossing film of 1997 as well as the ninth-highest-grossing film of the decade.

26
01:18:00,000 --> 01:18:06,000
It won for Best Makeup and was also nominated for Best Art Direction and Best
Original Score at the 70th Academy Awards, among numerous other accolades.

27
01:21:00,000 --> 01:21:06,000
A sequel was released in 2002, a third film was released in 2012, and a
stand-alone sequel was released in 2019, with Jones and Smith absent.

28
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
The film explores themes of release from prison, on the run,
wedding, woman director, bank robbery attempt.

29
01:27:00,000 --> 01:27:06,000
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
